nullAccessorDeref -- A BARE ACCESSOR THAT LAWFULLY ANSWERS NULL SEGFAULTS INSTEAD.

Minted 2026-09-25 by Clay's dispatch (date the countPop crash), which authorised the
mint. Found because countPop's repaired instrument showed all 47 probes dying.

THE MECHANISM, measured. opDot's accessor switch has seven cases that answer null when
there is nothing to answer with: parenT with no parent, registrY with no registry, nexT
on the LAST member, prioR on the FIRST, firsT and lasT on an empty list, and the first
member (405) with none. Null is the right answer in every one. After the switch opDot
runs `if !product.data product.count = 0;` -- WITHOUT asking whether product exists --
and dereferences the null. The very next line, `if product && !product.parent`, does
ask. One guard present, one missing, side by side (Instruct.rtn, opDot's tail).

